    <h1>Omnichannel Loyalty &amp; Growth Strategy</h1>
    <p class="project-subtitle" style="text-align: center; color: var(--color-muted); margin-bottom: 2rem;">Scaling CVS ExtraCare &amp; ExtraCare Plus Across 80M+ Members</p>

    <!-- Executive Scorecard -->
    <div class="project-meta-list">
      <p><span class="meta-label">Leadership Role:</span> Lead Product Designer &amp; Growth Strategist</p>
      <p><span class="meta-label">Scale &amp; Reach:</span> 80M+ Active Members across 9,000+ Stores, Self-Checkout &amp; Mobile</p>
      <p><span class="meta-label">Cross-Functional Partners:</span> VP of Loyalty &amp; Personalization, CRM Marketing, Store Operations, Retail Engineering</p>
      <p><span class="meta-label">Core Business Impact:</span> Generated <strong>$60M in incremental annual margin</strong>, unlocked <strong>+25,000 new weekly enrollments</strong>, and unified reward mechanics across 4 distinct software platforms.</p>
    </div>

    <p class="project-intro">As design lead for the Loyalty and Consumer Growth track, my goal was to turn routine checkout transactions into long-term customer relationships. By identifying where shoppers were dropping off and simplifying clunky registration requirements, my team optimized enrollment, member retention, and customer lifetime value across both our in-store registers and digital apps.</p>

    <h2>Initiative 1: Frictionless Single-Data-Point Enrollment</h2>

    <h3>The Problem</h3>
    <p>Around 54% of all in-store transactions at CVS happen at Self-Checkout (SCO). But roughly 60% of those transactions were completely unlinked to an ExtraCare account. At the time, the self-checkout screen didn't highlight the savings customers were missing, nor did it offer a quick way to sign up. If a shopper wanted member pricing, they had to abandon their checkout lane, track down a store associate to enroll them on a separate terminal, or just forfeit their discounts. That friction resulted in massive drop-off.</p>

    <h3>The Strategy &amp; Alignment</h3>
    <p>I led the redesign of the self-checkout onboarding flow with one radical constraint: <strong>make enrollment require only a single, high-intent piece of data—the customer's phone number.</strong></p>

    <p>Getting this approved required close partnership with our fraud, loss prevention, and retail operations teams. To satisfy security without adding friction at the lane, we designed a split onboarding architecture: collect the phone number instantly in-lane to unlock immediate cart discounts, validate via one-time SMS pin, and defer the rest of the profile setup (email, home address, communication preferences) to a follow-up digital touchpoint on web or mobile.</p>

