    <h2>Initiative 2: In-Lane Subscription Upgrade (ExtraCare Plus)</h2>

    <h3>The Problem</h3>
    <p>ExtraCare Plus is CVS’s paid monthly membership tier. Historically, signing up in a store was completely detached from the checkout process. If a shopper decided to join while buying items, the cashier had to void the entire cart transaction, run a separate membership onboarding workflow, and then re-scan every item from scratch. Because this created lines and frustrated shoppers, store associates actively discouraged customers from signing up.</p>

    <h3>The Solution</h3>
    <p>I re-architected the subscription upgrade to live natively inside the regular basket transaction. Working directly with our POS software engineering team, we treated the paid membership as an active register SKU. A customer could tap to join, have the monthly fee added right to their running total, and see their newly unlocked ExtraCare Plus discounts applied to the very items in their hands before paying.</p>

    <h3>The Impact</h3>
    <p>We turned an awkward, multi-step void-and-restart process into a seamless one-tap decision. Cashiers became advocates instead of blockers, and in-store conversion for ExtraCare Plus increased dramatically.</p>

