    <h2>Initiative 3: Unifying Rewards Across 4 Software Platforms</h2>

    <h3>The Challenge</h3>
    <p>The Pharmacy Rewards program had high customer interest, but the user experience was fragmented across four distinct technical ecosystems: in-store cashier terminals, self-checkout kiosks, the CVS mobile app, and CVS.com. Customers rarely knew how close they were to earning a reward, and store associates struggled to explain how family accounts linked together.</p>

    <h3>The Solution</h3>
    <p>I designed a modular reward framework that created visual and interaction parity across all four platforms. Together with front-end engineering, we established synchronized design tokens for tracking progress bars, active earned credits, and redemption prompts.</p>

    <p>We audited the customer journey to address three major gaps:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Customer Transparency:</strong> Shifted critical reward tracking from colleague-only back-office views to customer-facing screens.</li>
      <li><strong>Family Account Linking:</strong> Designed clear account management modals that eliminated colleague confusion around multi-member households.</li>
      <li><strong>Celebration Moments:</strong> Introduced joyful confirmation moments when rewards were issued, encouraging immediate re-engagement in the retail aisles.</li>
    </ul>

