    <h2>Initiative 4: In-App Gamification &amp; Habit Building</h2>
    <p>While ExtraCare had massive passive enrollment, our digital team wanted to encourage daily active use. I led the product design for CVS’s interactive gamification features, introducing digital punch cards and milestone achievements that reward customers for healthy micro-habits and repeat shopping trips.</p>

    <p>To ensure this wasn't an isolated screen inside the app, I worked closely with our marketing and store experience partners to align in-app animations directly with push notifications, email campaigns, and in-store signage.</p>

    <h2>Leadership Retrospective</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Friction is Expensive:</strong> Requiring customers to fill out 7 form fields at a checkout terminal was costing CVS tens of millions in lost lifetime value. Simplifying the input down to a single phone number was one of the highest-leverage design decisions we made.</li>
      <li><strong>Design Must Partner with Fraud &amp; Loss Prevention:</strong> Growth design in retail isn't just about funnels; it requires building logic that defends against abuse, duplicates, and cashier workarounds without punishing honest customers.</li>
      <li><strong>True Omnichannel Requires Shared Tech Governance:</strong> You cannot deliver a seamless loyalty experience if the app team, web team, and POS team operate in silos. Establishing a shared component library was the glue that made this launch successful.</li>
    </ol>
